   "text": "I read this as a cyclic depsipeptide and transcribed it residue by residue. Stereochemistry comes from the wedges and hashes, which I checked centre by centre.\n\n**Ring residues, in order around the macrocycle:**\n1. L-proline: the ring N is acylated by the Leu carbonyl, and its carbonyl links to the N-methyl nitrogen of the next residue.\n2. N-methyl-O-methyl-L-tyrosine: its carboxyl forms an ester with the threonine oxygen.\n3. Threonine: the ester O sits on the beta carbon. The alpha NH carries an exocyclic N-methyl-leucine, and its carbonyl is linked to the next residue.\n4. A 4-amino-3-hydroxy-5-methylheptanoic acid unit (isostatine-type): the amino group is on C4, OH on C3 and the methyl on C5. Its carboxyl is joined to the next residue.\n5. \u03b1-Aminoisobutyric acid (Aib, a gem-dimethyl residue): its carbonyl is joined to the next residue.\n6. L-leucine: its NH is acylated by Aib, and its carbonyl closes the ring onto the proline nitrogen.\n\n**Stereocentres, assigned from the drawing:** Pro is L, Leu is L, and N-Me-Tyr(OMe) is L. Thr, the C3, C4 and C5 centres of the isostatine unit, and the exocyclic N-Me-Leu were each worked out from their hashed or wedged bonds.\n\nI wrote the SMILES with label 1 for the macrocycle closure and label 2 for the proline ring.\n\nSMILES: N12CCC[C@H]2C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OC)cc2)C(=O)O[C@H](C)[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H](CC(C)C)NC)C(=O)N[C@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@@H](O)CC(=O)NC(C)(C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C1=O"
